# SecLogTrace .gitignore
#
# Pilot-/experiment-scale raw and processed data stays committed (decision
# 2026-08-21) so small datasets are usable from any machine. BUT at CORPUS
# scale this does not hold: the 5-class corpus raw Jaeger is ~1.2 GB and the
# processed span tables ~268 MB (mostly per-service export duplication +
# NacosWatch noise). Committing that to git history is impractical, so as of
# 2026-09-04 (option A) the bulk is archived SEPARATELY (Zenodo/Figshare, for
# the Paper A / MSR data-showcase DOI release) and ignored here. What STAYS in
# git: trace feature tables (data/processed/combined/), traffic session logs
# (data/raw/traffic/), and per-trace log features (logs_by_trace.csv) — the
# reproducible, citable core. Already-committed pilot data is unaffected.
data/raw/jaeger/
data/raw/logs/
data/processed/traces/
data/processed/logs/**/logs.csv
data/processed/logs/**/_raw/

# Python bytecode -- never useful to commit, and two stray .pyc files
# were already tracked before this file existed (removed 2026-08-21).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Local virtual environments, if one is ever created here
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Jupyter checkpoints, if notebooks are ever added
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS-generated cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor/IDE settings not shared with the team
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local secrets -- never commit these even if one shows up
.env
*.pem
*.key
